# Team

**Aescia is being built by a small team with direct experience in acute clinical environments, health technology, and regulated software development.**

---

## Founding team

### James Kurrle — Founder and Clinical Lead

James has clinical and operational experience in acute care environments. The Aescia platform concept is grounded in direct clinical observation of the post-discharge gap — patients who deteriorate after discharge before structured follow-up reaches them.

Aescia's design reflects that experience: the platform is built around clinical workflow reality, not theoretical efficiency.

**Contact:** james@aesciahealth.com

---

## Technical and compliance

Aescia's technical development is led by specialists with experience in regulated health software environments. The platform's architecture and development practices are aligned to IEC 62304 software lifecycle principles and ISO 27001 information security standards, reflecting the requirements of clinical and regulated environments.

---

## Clinical and governance input

Aescia is being developed with input from clinicians, technical specialists, and governance advisors with experience in digital health, clinical governance, and healthcare regulation.

Where advisors are in a position to be publicly named, their details will be published here. In the interim, Aescia will not imply named institutional backing or advisory roles without explicit permission.

